<p>"Memories" is a change of pace from the run of stories before it — a photo album section, spanning printed pp.97–112 of the book, built almost entirely of snapshots and their captions rather than narrative prose. Every caption, year label and name John printed beneath each photo is transcribed exactly as printed, in the order it appears; where the book gave a photo its own printed header — a year, a title in quotation marks — that header is kept as the lead of the caption below it.</p>

