  <div class="source-doc-poem">
    <p>
      It's no big deal that our chests have slipped<br>
      and tri-focals grace our eyes<br>
      Or that we struggle for equilibrium<br>
      and forget to zip our flies
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="source-doc-image">
    <img src="/images/site/echoes-memories-author-chuck-davlin.jpg" alt="Black-and-white photograph of two men talking underground in a mine, one wearing a miner's cap lamp and work clothes, the other in a light jacket.">
    <figcaption>The author &amp; Charles "Chuck" Davlin.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="source-doc-poem">
    <p>
      Deep underground, in cold confines, we met to chart our course<br>
      to sample nature's treasures, perhaps, to find the source<br><br>
      The silent rocks listened to us within their complex state<br>
      and hid the gold we lusted for but assured us of our fate
    </p>
  </div>
